      "narrative": "Mara's eyebrows lift slightly at your question\u2014a flicker of interest, like she's reassessing you.\n\n\"Already putting pieces together. Good.\" She taps a finger on the table. \"Toran Vex. That's your man\u2014the one nursing his tea at the bar with the ink-stained cuffs. He's been the lockwright for the Ash Gate for the better part of a decade. Sworn to the Kestrel Guild, bound by their oaths, the whole ceremony.\"\n\nShe glances over at him. He's hunched over a chipped mug, not drinking, just staring into it like it holds answers.\n\n\"He maintained that lock personally. Every month, without fail. Oiled the tumblers, tested the sequence, logged it in the Guild ledger.\" Her voice tightens. \"And the day *before* the seal order came down, he signed off on it. Declared it sound. Functioning. Secure.\"\n\nShe turns back to you, a hard edge in her voice. \"So either Toran Vex is a liar, or someone got to that lock without him knowing\u2014someone who knew his work well enough to slip past every safeguard he'd built.\"\n\nShe lets the question hang. \"Which one do you think it is?\""
    },
