      "narrative": "Rain hits your face as you push through the Finch's door. The street is empty\u2014grey cobbles, shuttered windows, a single dog trotting past with its tail low. The Ash Gate stands at the end of the lane, a cracked black arch against the pale morning sky.\n\nFifty paces. Thirty. The air changes as you approach\u2014colder, stiller, carrying a faint mineral scent like wet stone and rust. The Gate looms, its surface webbed with hairline fractures, the massive lock mechanism bolted to its center. A fresh seal of black iron and Guild wax hangs from the hasp, unbroken.\n\nThe ground around the arch is churned with footprints\u2014boot prints, some fresh, pressed into the mud within the last few hours. They lead to the Gate's base, then stop. As if whoever made them simply... vanished.\n\nA loose cobble near the left pillar catches your eye. It sits slightly higher than the others, the mortar around it cracked and dark.\n\nThe Gate stands silent. The footprints wait. The cobble offers."
    },
