      "narrative": "You step closer to the Gate, the cracked arch swallowing the grey light above you. You fill your lungs and call out.\n\n\"Old Bram!\"\n\nYour voice rings off the stone\u2014sharp, clear\u2014then dies into the wet air. No echo. No reply. The sound seems to hit the Gate's surface and simply stop, absorbed like water into dry sand.\n\nSilence settles back. Thick. Heavy. The kind of silence that has weight.\n\nA gust of wind stirs past you, carrying ash from somewhere\u2014no fires lit in this district, not at this hour. It curls across the churned ground, picking at the edges of the footprints.\n\nNothing moves. Nothing answers.\n\nThe Gate stands sealed. The loose cobble waits near the left pillar. And behind you, at the end of the lane, a figure in a travel-stained cloak steps out from a recessed doorway, watching."
