      "narrative": "You crouch low, scanning the cobblestones beneath the arch. Your fingers brush the wet stone, tracing the cracks, the worn edges, the places where generations of boots have scuffed the surface. Nothing. Just weather and age and the slow grind of time against worked stone.\n\nThe loose cobble near the left pillar catches your attention again, but the more you look at it, the more ordinary it seems. A stone that shifted from rain and frost. Cracked mortar. Not a hiding place\u2014just wear.\n\nYou straighten up, mud on your knees, nothing in your hands.\n\nAt the end of the lane, the cloaked figure still watches. They haven't moved. Haven't called out. Just stand there, a dark shape against the grey street, arms folded beneath their stained cloak."
