      "narrative": "The Copper Finch's door groans shut behind you, cutting the chill. The tavern is busier now\u2014a few more patrons have drifted in, hunched over morning ale, speaking in low murmurs. Smoke curls from a pipe near the hearth. The air smells of old beer, damp wool, and woodsmoke.\n\nYour table is where you left it. A scarred oak slab near the back wall, the surface crosshatched with knife marks and candle wax. You settle onto the bench, the wood creaking under you.\n\nMara Venn is still at the bar. She's turned on her stool, a half-empty cup in her hand, and she's watching you with those sharp, appraising eyes. She doesn't call over\u2014just watches, waiting to see what you'll do next.\n\nNear the hearth, a nervous man with ink-stained cuffs clutches a mug, staring into its depths. Toran Vex. The lockwright. He hasn't noticed you come in."
